@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+# US-08: Train as a background job
+
+| | |
+| --- | --- |
+| Epic | WBMME-2 Model Training & Selection |
+| Requirement | MLE-F-009 (also MLE-F-005, MLE-F-006 for the data steps) |
+| Points / sprint | 8 / Sprint 1 |
+| Owner | Varnika (Member 2) |
+| SAD component | Model Selection & Training |
+
+**Story.** As a Data Scientist I want training to run in the background, so that the page stays usable while a model trains and I can check the status later.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- [x] `POST /api/train` returns `202` at once with a run ID and never waits for training.
+- [x] A run moves Queued -> Running -> Completed or Failed, with start and finish times.
+- [x] A job runs in its own thread (or inline when `WBMME_JOBS_INLINE` is set, which tests use).
+- [x] The trained pipeline is saved in a per-user folder outside the web root, written atomically.
+- [x] Problems with the data (missing target, wrong number of classes, class with one row, test share too small) fail the run with a plain message.
+- [x] Internal errors are logged on the server; the user sees a generic message only.
+- [x] A user can only read their own runs, and only train on their own datasets; another user's ID answers `404`.
+- [x] Missing values and categories are handled inside the pipeline, fitted on the training split only (no data leakage).
+- [x] The split is stratified and repeatable for the same test share and seed.
+
+## Files
+
+| File | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `training/models.py`, `migrations/0001_initial.py` | `TrainingRun` record |
+| `training/pipeline.py` | Pure-Python load, check, split and fit |
+| `training/schemas.py` | Validation of the request body |
+| `training/jobs.py` | `submit` and `execute_run` |
+| `training/artifacts.py` | Per-user atomic artifact storage |
+| `training/locator.py` | Placeholder dataset lookup (replaced by US-01 storage, see INTEGRATION.md) |
+| `training/views.py`, `urls.py` | `POST /api/train`, `GET /api/train/<id>` |
+| `training/tests/test_pipeline.py`, `test_api_train.py` | 43 tests |
+
+## API
+
+```
+POST /api/train
+{"dataset_id": 1, "target": "species", "model": "random_forest",
+ "params": {"n_estimators": 50}, "test_size": 0.2, "seed": 42}
+
+202 {"run_id": 7, "status": "queued", "status_url": "/api/train/7"}
+
+GET /api/train/7
+200 {"run_id": 7, "status": "completed", "model": "random_forest", "duration_seconds": 0.8, ...}
+```
+
+## Design notes (for the viva)
+
+- A thread is the simplest thing that satisfies "background" for a single-server student project. US-21 moves the work into a separate process so a crash or hang cannot take down the web server.
+- Preprocessing lives inside the scikit-learn Pipeline so the test split never influences the fitted imputer or scaler.
